```php
<?php

namespace CloudStoragePackage;

use GuzzleHttp\Client;
use GuzzleHttp\Psr7\Request;
use League\Flysystem\AdapterInterface;
use League\Flysystem\Filesystem;

class CloudStoragePackage {
    private $fileSystems = [];
    private $apiClients = [];

    public function __construct(array $config) {
        foreach ($config as $service => $credentials) {
            $this->fileSystems[$service] = $this->getFilesystem($service, $credentials);
            $this->apiClients[$service] = $this->getApiClient($service, $credentials);
        }
    }

    private function getFilesystem(string $service, array $credentials): Filesystem {
        return new Filesystem(new AdapterInterface());
    }

    private function getApiClient(string $service, array $credentials): Client {
        return new Client([
            'base_uri' => $credentials['api_endpoint'],
            'timeout' => 30.0,
            // ... other Guzzle options ...
        ]);
    }

    public function uploadFile(string $file, string $service): void {
        $this->fileSystems[$service]->put($file, file_get_contents($file));
    }

    public function downloadFile(string $file, string $service): void {
        $content = $this->fileSystems[$service]->get($file);
        file_put_contents($file, $content);
    }
}

```

This code is a starting point for creating a modular PHP package that interfaces with multiple cloud-based storage services. It uses the League\Flysystem library to manage file systems and the GuzzleHttp\Client library to interact with APIs.

The `CloudStoragePackage` class takes an array of configuration settings for each cloud storage service, initializes file systems and API clients for each service, and provides methods for uploading and downloading files between the local file system and the cloud storage services.

This package can be extended to support additional features such as asynchronous operations, version control, and audit logging. It also needs to be integrated with an existing enterprise-level application architecture, which currently uses a monolithic database and relies on a custom API gateway for request handling.

Note that this is just one possible implementation of the required functionality, and you may need to modify or extend it based on your specific requirements."]

